    { id: 'buying-or-selling-property-in-phase-5', h: 'Why This Matters Specifically If You\'re Buying or Selling in DHA Phase 5', body: `<p>Property transactions in DHA Phase 5, like anywhere else, carry a withholding tax rate that differs sharply between filers and non-filers — for a property in this price range, that difference is rarely small. Registering for an NTN before finalizing a purchase or sale, rather than scrambling once the transaction is already in motion, is worth doing with enough lead time that the registration is fully processed before it's actually needed at the registrar's office or the bank.</p>` },
    { id: 'common-mistakes-in-this-area', h: 'Mistakes That Specifically Trip Up DHA Phase 5 Applicants', body: `<p>The most common issue is an address format mismatch — writing the DHA plot/street reference one way on the utility bill and a slightly different way on the IRIS application, which can cause an otherwise straightforward registration to be flagged for manual review and delayed. Double-checking that the address entered matches the utility bill exactly, down to the sector and street formatting DHA itself uses, avoids this entirely preventable holdup.</p>` },
    { id: 'what-happens-after-registration', h: 'What Happens Right After You\'re Registered', body: `<p>Once your NTN is issued, you're expected to file an annual income tax return going forward — registration itself doesn't require an immediate filing, but it does start the clock on the obligation for the tax year you're registered in. Many DHA Phase 5 residents register and file their first return in the same sitting, since the same documentation (CNIC, address proof, income details) largely carries over.</p>` },
    { id: 'checking-your-atl-status-after-dha-registration', h: 'Confirming Your Active Taxpayer List Status Once Registered', body: `<p>Registration alone doesn't automatically make you an active filer with the lower withholding rate — that status comes once your return for the relevant year is actually filed and processed. A DHA Phase 5 resident who registers close to a property transaction should confirm their ATL status has genuinely updated before relying on it for that specific transaction, rather than assuming registration alone is enough on the day it happens.</p>` },
    { id: 'dha-phase-5-vs-neighboring-phases', h: 'Does It Matter Which Specific DHA Phase Borders Phase 5', body: `<p>The underlying NTN process is identical regardless of which specific DHA phase you're in — Phase 5 residents sometimes ask whether being adjacent to a different phase changes anything, and it doesn't. What matters for registration purposes is your actual documented address, not the phase number itself or its position relative to neighboring phases.</p>` },
    { id: 'kamboh-help', h: 'How Kamboh Associates Helps DHA Phase 5 Residents', body: `<p>We handle NTN registration for DHA Phase 5 residents entirely over WhatsApp — send your CNIC and a recent utility bill or possession letter, and we take care of the IRIS submission, including catching the address-formatting details that specifically trip up DHA applications. Flat Rs. 2,000, no office visit needed.</p>` }
