    { q: 'Does registering an NTN for a small shop in E1 also require sales tax registration?', a: 'Not automatically — sales tax (STRN) registration is a separate, subsequent requirement that depends on the business\'s turnover and nature, worth understanding early rather than discovering later.' },
    { q: 'How long does NTN registration take for a Block E1 application?', a: 'A complete, well-documented individual or proprietorship application is often processed the same day, depending on FBR\'s own processing at the time.' },
    { q: 'What is the most common mistake business applicants in E1 make?', a: 'Providing an incomplete or inconsistent description of the business activity, which can slow down processing — being specific and accurate avoids this.' },
    { q: 'Does business income from an E1 shop get filed separately from personal income?', a: 'No — for a proprietorship, business income flows into the same personal annual return, not a separate company filing.' },
    { q: 'What is the most common mistake residential applicants in Block E1 make?', a: 'An address-formatting mismatch between the utility bill and the IRIS entry, which can flag the application for manual review.' },
    { q: 'How much does NTN registration cost through Kamboh Associates?', a: 'A flat Rs. 2,000 for both residential and small business proprietorship registrations, handled entirely over WhatsApp.' },
    { q: 'Can Kamboh Associates help figure out if my E1 business also needs sales tax registration?', a: 'Yes — we assess your specific turnover and business activity and advise whether STRN registration applies before it becomes an unexpected requirement.' },
    { q: 'Is same-day NTN issuance realistic for a Block E1 business registration?', a: 'Often yes for a complete, well-documented proprietorship application, though this isn\'t guaranteed and depends on FBR\'s own processing volume.' },
    { q: 'Does a Block E1 resident with no business need anything different from a standard individual registration?', a: 'No — a purely residential applicant follows the standard individual NTN process with no business-specific documentation needed.' },
    { q: 'What if my Block E1 shop\'s address is different from where I personally live?', a: 'That\'s fine — the business address and your personal residential address can be different, and both should be accurately reflected in the relevant parts of the registration.' },
    { q: 'Does it matter if my E1 shop premises are rented rather than owned?', a: 'No — this doesn\'t affect NTN registration itself, though having your lease agreement on hand as supporting context for the business address is worth doing.' },
    { q: 'Should I register for an NTN before or after actually opening my new Block E1 business?', a: 'Before, ideally — registering before you start trading establishes your tax position from day one and avoids a gap between when the business actually started and when it was formally registered.' },
    { q: 'My Block E1 shop is jointly run by two partners — do we both need our own NTN?', a: 'Yes — each partner generally needs their own NTN, and depending on the partnership structure, the business may need its own separate AOP registration, worth confirming specifically.' },
    { q: 'Does Kamboh Associates handle NTN registration for other Johar Town blocks too, not just E1?', a: 'Yes — Block E1 is just one of many Johar Town blocks we regularly register clients from; the process is the same across the neighborhood.' },
    { q: 'Can a Block E1 online seller register using the same personal documentation as a residential applicant?', a: 'Yes — an online-only business uses the same core CNIC, mobile number, and email details, with the business activity simply noted on the application.' }
