    { q: 'Does Faisal Town\'s older housing stock cause any specific issues with NTN registration?', a: 'It can, mainly around utility bills still being in a previous owner\'s or relative\'s name — this is workable, but worth flagging clearly upfront rather than discovering it mid-application.' },
    { q: 'Does the type of business I run on Faisal Town\'s commercial frontage affect the registration process?', a: 'No — a tuition center, a clinic, and a repair shop all follow an identical registration process, differing only in how the business activity is described on the application.' },
    { q: 'My parent\'s Faisal Town business is passing to me — do I need a new NTN or can I use theirs?', a: 'A genuine ownership transfer generally means you need your own registration reflecting the business going forward, rather than continuing to operate under your parent\'s existing NTN indefinitely.' },
    { q: 'I run a small home-based business from my Faisal Town home — do I need to register for an NTN?', a: 'If it\'s become a meaningful, regular income source rather than an occasional hobby, yes — home-based activity isn\'t exempt from the usual registration rules once that threshold is reasonably crossed.' },
    { q: 'I\'ve been renting out part of my Faisal Town house informally for years without registering — is it too late?', a: 'No — there\'s no penalty for coming forward now; registering and properly declaring the rental income going forward is what matters, regardless of how long the informal arrangement has been in place.' },
    { q: 'Does it matter if my Faisal Town rental arrangement is informal, without a written lease?', a: 'Not for NTN registration itself — the income is what\'s taxable regardless of how formal the paperwork is, though a documented lease can make the later filing process cleaner.' },
    { q: 'I own more than one rented property in Faisal Town — does each one need separate handling on my NTN?', a: 'No — one NTN covers you as an individual regardless of how many properties you own; each property\'s rental income simply gets declared together under your single registration when you file.' },
    { q: 'Does Kamboh Associates handle both the residential and small-business side of NTN registration in the same visit to Faisal Town clients?', a: 'We work entirely over WhatsApp rather than visiting in person, and yes — a single engagement can cover a personal registration, a business registration, or both together for the same client.' }
